  "notes": "USAGE:\n{侍|さむらい} refers to members of the warrior class in feudal Japan. In modern usage, it is often used figuratively or in cultural contexts such as film titles and sports nicknames.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {武士|ぶし}: warrior (more formal, historical term)\n- {武士道|ぶしどう}: the way of the warrior, bushido\n- {刀|かたな}: sword\n- {殿様|とのさま}: feudal lord\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {侍|さむらい}{魂|だましい}: samurai spirit\n- {侍|さむらい}ジャパン: Samurai Japan (national sports teams)\n- {侍|さむらい}{映画|えいが}: samurai film",
